!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/class2/schema/valid/an-enum-draws-its-labels-from-a-vocabulary-the-schema-declares-expected.tn"
!!schema:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/schema-sidecar.tn"
{
  spec: "[TSON-SCHEMA] §7.4"
  description: """
    `enum_type` is the constructor `enum` and `text_enum` tighten, and it takes `type` as data: any
    text family, written by the author and resolved in the author's own namespace. So an ordinary
    schema, which may not declare a constructor, can still enumerate the labels of a naming
    vocabulary it declares itself. Each member must be a value of `type` -- here an identifier
    matching `kebab`'s pattern -- and since `kebab` is an `identifier_type` instance, the members are
    names and [TSON-DATA] §8.2's hygiene reaches them.
    """
  meta: "meta.tn"
  import: ["core.tn"]
  valid: {
    resolved: """
      !schema {
        kebab => !type_definition {
          source: identifier_type
          body: !identifier_type { continue_add: "-"  pattern: "[a-z]+(-[a-z]+)*" }
        }

        steps => !type_definition {
          source: enum_type
          body: !enum_type { name_type: kebab  members: [make-tea drink-tea] }
        }
      }
      """
  }
}
